{"event": "created", "monotonic_ns": 1238147916306159, "wall_time_ns": 1791904248919685292, "thresholds": {"seed": 42, "instance": 21, "ros_domain_id": 71, "agent_port": 18888, "startup_timeout_s": 90, "takeoff_timeout_s": 45, "landing_timeout_s": 60, "hover_s": 10, "neural_s": 5, "repetitions": 3, "altitude_m": 3, "hover_max_error_m": 1.0, "hover_max_tilt_deg": 15, "safety_radius_m": 10, "safety_altitude_m": 8, "safety_tilt_deg": 45, "safety_angular_rate_rad_s": 8, "inference_p99_us": 2500, "settling_band_m": 0.2, "settling_dwell_s": 2.0, "joint_recovery": {"position_reference": "active_controller_target", "position_reference_note": "Same rule as P0 (the controller's own position target), extended to RAPTOR: its internal target is not published on trajectory_setpoint, so while RAPTOR owns the actuators the target is its logged capture (activation reset or setpoint-stale hold); classic stages use trajectory_setpoint as in P0. trajectory_setpoint-only and fixed NED results are kept as comparisons.", "position_reference_ned_m": [0, 0, -3], "velocity_reference_ned_m_s": [0, 0, 0], "angular_velocity_reference_frd_rad_s": [0, 0, 0], "position_threshold_m": 0.2, "velocity_threshold_m_s": 0.1, "angular_velocity_threshold_rad_s": 0.1, "dwell_s": 2.0, "max_observation_gap_s": 0.02}, "p0_strict": true, "p1": {"conditions": {"S1": {"speed_m_s": 0.0, "description": "stable hover"}, "S2": {"speed_m_s": 0.5, "description": "low-speed horizontal motion"}, "S3": {"speed_m_s": 1.0, "description": "moderate horizontal motion"}}, "speed_rationale": "Requested starting values kept. Travel along +N is accel_s*v/2 + cruise_s*v (S3: 5.0 m, S2: 2.5 m) plus braking; the worst case stays below 7 m, leaving at least 3 m to the frozen 10 m safety radius, and 0.5 m/s^2 ramp acceleration is gentle for both controllers.", "motion_axis_ned": [1, 0, 0], "reference_hold_s": 3.0, "accel_s": 2.0, "cruise_s": 4.0, "offboard_prestream_s": 1.0, "setpoint_period_s": 0.02, "post_handover_s": 10.0, "return_hold_s": 8.0, "reference": "Before the subject event the outgoing controller tracks one runner-published trajectory_setpoint (position ramp, velocity and acceleration feed-forward, constant yaw) starting from its own current target: classic through OFFBOARD, RAPTOR through its external trajectory_setpoint input. At the event the stream stops and the incoming controller uses its original mechanism: RAPTOR mode-entry reset holds the activation position/yaw with zero velocity; classic AUTO_LOITER brakes to the navigator loiter point.", "baselines": "p1_baseline_classic: classic OFFBOARD motion then AUTO_LOITER (same takeover mechanism, no controller switch). p1_baseline_raptor: RAPTOR external-setpoint motion then the stream stops; after RAPTOR's 200 ms setpoint timeout it holds its position (same capture rule as mode entry, no reset or switch).", "handover_repetitions": 5, "baseline_repetitions": 3, "motor_saturation": {"upper": 0.999, "lower": 0.001, "note": "actuator_motors control in [0,1]; upper/lower limit within 1e-3"}, "motor_step_window_s": [-0.1, 0.5]}, "p1_condition": "S3", "p1_speed_m_s": 1.0}}
